IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part I, "Special Benefits": ss 21 (illness, injury or quarantine) and
-- 22 (pregnancy). Layer 1 of piece ei1. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30. A week is identified by the DATE of its Sunday (the core); a period is a `Period of days`.
--
-- "Reduced or eliminated as prescribed" (s 21(2), s 22(3)): the Regulations deposited prescribe a reduction for benefits
-- under s 22 or 23 where provincial benefits are paid under a provincial plan (regs 76.16 and 76.17, piece er4); none was
-- found for s 21(2). In both cases the reduction is an input: the amount by which the benefits are reduced.

§ `Section 21 - illness, injury or quarantine`

-- src:483 | 21 (1) A minor attachment claimant who ceases work because of illness, injury or quarantine is not entitled to receive benefits while unable to work for that reason.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 21(1) (src:483)
GIVEN `the claimant is a minor attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant ceases work because of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is unable to work for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21(1) the minor attachment claimant is not entitled to receive benefits while unable to work for that reason` IF
        `the claimant is a minor attachment claimant`
    AND `the claimant ceases work because of illness, injury or quarantine`
    AND `the claimant is unable to work for that reason`

-- src:485 | (2) If benefits are payable to a claimant as a result of illness, injury or quarantine and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant for that illness, injury or quarantine under a provincial law, the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act shall be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 21(2) (src:485)
GIVEN `benefits are payable to the claimant as a result of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant for that illness, injury or quarantine under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount by which the regulations reduce the benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 21(2) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` IS
    IF `benefits are payable to the claimant as a result of illness, injury or quarantine`
       AND `any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant for that illness, injury or quarantine under a provincial law`
    THEN max 0 (`the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act` MINUS `the amount by which the regulations reduce the benefits`)
    ELSE `the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act`

-- src:487 | (3) Subject to subsection 19(3), if, as a result of illness, injury or quarantine, benefits are payable to a claimant for a week of unemployment, there shall be deducted from those benefits any allowances, money or other benefits payable to the claimant for that week under a plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer and in respect of which the employer’s premium has been reduced in accordance with regulations made under subsection 69(1).
-- The plan is one that covers insured persons employed by an employer and in respect of which the employer's premium has
-- been reduced under regulations made under subsection 69(1) (piece ei3). "Subject to subsection 19(3)" means that the
-- undeclared-earnings deduction of s 19(3) comes first.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 21(3) (src:487)
GIVEN `benefits are payable to the claimant for a week of unemployment as a result of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits payable for the week before the deduction` IS A NUMBER
      `the allowances, money or other benefits payable to the claimant for that week under a plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: section 69(1) and the regulations made under it (piece ei3, reg 62 and following in piece er4)
      `the employer's premium has been reduced in accordance with regulations made under subsection 69(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 21(3) the benefits payable for the week after deducting the allowances payable under the employer's plan` IS
    IF `benefits are payable to the claimant for a week of unemployment as a result of illness, injury or quarantine`
       AND `the employer's premium has been reduced in accordance with regulations made under subsection 69(1)`
    THEN max 0 (`the benefits payable for the week before the deduction` MINUS `the allowances, money or other benefits payable to the claimant for that week under a plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer`)
    ELSE `the benefits payable for the week before the deduction`

§ `Section 22 - pregnancy`

-- src:489 | 22 (1) Despite section 18, but subject to this section, benefits are payable to a major attachment claimant who proves her pregnancy.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 22(1) (src:489)
GIVEN `the claimant is a major attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant proves her pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22(1) benefits are payable to the claimant despite section 18` IF
        `the claimant is a major attachment claimant`
    AND `the claimant proves her pregnancy`

-- src:491 | (2) Subject to section 12, benefits are payable to a major attachment claimant under this section for each week of unemployment in the period
-- src:492 | (a) that begins the earlier of
-- src:493 | (i) 12 weeks before the week in which her confinement is expected, and
-- src:494 | (ii) the week in which her confinement occurs; and
-- src:495 | (b) that ends 17 weeks after the later of
-- src:496 | (i) the week in which her confinement is expected, and
-- src:497 | (ii) the week in which her confinement occurs.
-- The period begins on the first day of the earlier of (i) the week 12 weeks before the week in which her confinement is
-- expected and (ii) the week in which her confinement occurs, and ends on the last day of the week 17 weeks after the later of
-- the expected week and the week in which confinement occurs. Where confinement has not yet occurred only the expected
-- week is known and (ii) has nothing to measure. A date given is any day of the week it is in. Read as running to the last day
-- of the week 17 weeks after (fork F-22-2 in NOTES.md).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 22(2) (src:491-497)
GIVEN `a day in the week in which her confinement is expected` IS A DATE
      `a day in the week in which her confinement occurs, if it has occurred` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 22(2) the period during which benefits are payable` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the first day` , `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the Sunday of the week in which her confinement is expected` MEANS
            `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `a day in the week in which her confinement is expected`
        `the first day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `a day in the week in which her confinement occurs, if it has occurred`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the Sunday of the week in which her confinement is expected` MINUS `weeks as days` 12
            WHEN JUST occurred THEN
                IF `the Sunday of the week in which her confinement is expected` MINUS `weeks as days` 12 AT MOST `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` occurred
                THEN `the Sunday of the week in which her confinement is expected` MINUS `weeks as days` 12
                ELSE `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` occurred
        `the last day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `a day in the week in which her confinement occurs, if it has occurred`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (`the Sunday of the week in which her confinement is expected` PLUS `weeks as days` 17)
            WHEN JUST occurred THEN
                IF `the Sunday of the week in which her confinement is expected` AT LEAST `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` occurred
                THEN `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (`the Sunday of the week in which her confinement is expected` PLUS `weeks as days` 17)
                ELSE `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` occurred PLUS `weeks as days` 17)

-- src:499 | (3) When benefits are payable to a claimant for unemployment caused by pregnancy and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant for that pregnancy under a provincial law, the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act shall be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 22(3) (src:499)
GIVEN `benefits are payable to the claimant for unemployment caused by pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant for that pregnancy under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: regs 76.16 and 76.17 (piece er4)
      `the amount by which the regulations reduce the benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 22(3) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` IS
    IF `benefits are payable to the claimant for unemployment caused by pregnancy`
       AND `any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant for that pregnancy under a provincial law`
    THEN max 0 (`the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act` MINUS `the amount by which the regulations reduce the benefits`)
    ELSE `the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act`

-- src:501 | (4) For the purposes of section 13, the provisions of section 18 do not apply to the week that immediately precedes the period described in subsection (2).
-- The week immediately before the period of subsection (2) is the week that begins seven days before the period does.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 22(4) (src:501)
GIVEN `the period described in subsection (2)` IS A `Period of days`
      `the Sunday of the week in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22(4) section 18 does not apply, for the purposes of section 13, to the week` IF
    `the Sunday of the week in question` EQUALS `the period described in subsection (2)`'s `first day of the period` MINUS 7

-- src:503 | (5) Subject to subsection 19(3), if benefits are payable under this section to a major attachment claimant for a week of unemployment, there shall be deducted from those benefits any allowances, money or other benefits payable to the claimant for that week under a plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer and in respect of which the employer’s premium has been reduced in accordance with regulations made under subsection 69(1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 22(5) (src:503)
GIVEN `benefits are payable under section 22 to a major attachment claimant for a week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits payable for the week before the deduction` IS A NUMBER
      `the allowances, money or other benefits payable to the claimant for that week under a plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer` IS A NUMBER
      `the employer's premium has been reduced in accordance with regulations made under subsection 69(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 22(5) the benefits payable for the week after deducting the allowances payable under the employer's plan` IS
    IF `benefits are payable under section 22 to a major attachment claimant for a week of unemployment`
       AND `the employer's premium has been reduced in accordance with regulations made under subsection 69(1)`
    THEN max 0 (`the benefits payable for the week before the deduction` MINUS `the allowances, money or other benefits payable to the claimant for that week under a plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer`)
    ELSE `the benefits payable for the week before the deduction`

-- src:505 | (6) If a child who is born of the claimant’s pregnancy is hospitalized, the period during which benefits are payable under subsection (2) shall be extended by the number of weeks during which the child is hospitalized.
-- src:506 | Limitation
-- src:507 | (7) The extended period shall end no later than 52 weeks after the week of confinement.
-- The period is lengthened by the weeks the child is in hospital, but ends no later than the last day of the week
-- 52 weeks after the week of confinement.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 22(6), s 22(7) (src:505-507)
GIVEN `the period described in subsection (2)` IS A `Period of days`
      `the number of weeks during which the child born of the claimant's pregnancy is hospitalized` IS A NUMBER
      `a day in the week of confinement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 22(6) and s 22(7) the period during which benefits are payable, extended` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the period described in subsection (2)`'s `first day of the period`, `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS
            IF `the period described in subsection (2)`'s `last day of the period` PLUS `weeks as days` `the number of weeks during which the child born of the claimant's pregnancy is hospitalized` AT MOST `the latest last day`
            THEN `the period described in subsection (2)`'s `last day of the period` PLUS `weeks as days` `the number of weeks during which the child born of the claimant's pregnancy is hospitalized`
            ELSE `the latest last day`
        `the latest last day` MEANS
            `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `a day in the week of confinement` PLUS `weeks as days` 52)
